// lib/battle/problems.ts
//
// Code Battle's problem bank. Every testCases entry was generated by
// actually running a reference implementation (not hand-computed) — see
// the generation script referenced in the PR/commit for this file if the
// numbers ever look suspicious.
//
// Deliberately scoped to problems with a single, unambiguous correct
// output (numbers, strings, booleans, or an array with one valid order)
// so the judge can do a plain deep-equality check — no partial credit,
// no "any valid answer" logic. That's a real constraint on which
// problems can go in this bank: e.g. a Two Sum here specifies "return
// indices in ascending order" precisely so it stays exact-match judgeable
// even though a hashmap solution could otherwise return either order.
//
// NEVER import this file into client code — testCases.*.expected is the
// answer key. Only server-side routes (create/submit) may touch it.

